    "The deterministic unit-test fixtures write 2,024,160 bytes with binary sort merging versus 1,354,191 with eight-way merging; partitioned aggregation writes 471,040 versus 5,840,368 for sorted updates.",
    "Sort targets below 64 KiB use compact records; larger budgets admit typed blocks and their decoded merge workspace."
